:::profileBio

  I am a PhD student at the National University of Singapore, advised by [Ilya Sergey](https://ilyasergey.net). I am also a member of [LeanFRO](https://lean-lang.org/fro/) where I am building tools for reasoning about monadic Lean code.

  My research focuses on building scalable, trustworthy verification frameworks. I have contributed to
  * [Velvet](https://github.com/verse-lab/velvet), a Dafny-style multi-modal verifier
  * [Loom](https://github.com/verse-lab/loom), a library for reasoning about monadic Lean programs
  * [Veil](https://github.com/verse-lab/veil), a framework for distributed protocol verification
  * [B3](https://github.com/dafny-lang/b3), an SMT-based intermediate verification language, successor of [Boogie](https://github.com/boogie-org/boogie)


:::

# Important fact

In general, people tend to use _Vlad_ as a shortened version of my name. However, that is [incorrect](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vladimir_(name)). If you want to use *accurate* short forms for my name, they would be:

 * Vova (_Most common_)
 * Volodya (_Most formal_)
 * Mira (_Most unusual_)
 * Vovan (_Most informal_)
